Z||000000||Ayrhead||11-10-2000||09:57 AM||||Does anyone have a step by step procedure on how to change a clutch on an 86 Fiero 4 Cylinder? I already have a Haynes manual but it is still not explicate enough....||||reg||5
Z||000001||Old Lar||11-10-2000||11:33 AM||||What I do is take car to transmission shop and say I need a new clutch.  Sit in waiting room, drink coffee and read old Road and Track magazines.  Pay bill and drive home.||||reg||3
Z||000002||onfire||11-10-2000||01:13 PM||||That method was too expensive for me. I talkd to a couple of shops. One of the <BR>shops said they wouldn't even look at it. The other shop said $750 and I could pick it up<BR>in a few days. So me and my uncle did it, it still took two days but all it cost was the price of the clutch $115. <P>We did this at an apt. building so the cradle was left in. We took the wheels, axles, and disconnected every thing from the <BR>trany. We couldn't get the tran. out (a few more inches) but we did get the clutch in.<BR>It took some fancy manuevering and a little luck but we got it back together.<p>[This message has been edited by onfire (edited 11-10-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||2xsess||11-10-2000||01:20 PM||||ok, I found link for you that posts the step-by-step instructions of Mr Ed Parks.<P>Here ya go <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR> <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Archives/Archive-000001/HTML/20000815-2-001640.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Archives/Archive-000001/HTML/20000815-2-001640.html</A> <P>Good Luck.<P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/My_car_(large)sig_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||Chance||11-11-2000||07:31 AM||||Well, about a year and a half ago, my clutch went out, so I took it to who I thought were very good mechanics... paid 1200 bucks for "heavy duty clutch" a new flywheel, new master cly. etc. recently, had problems shifting, took it back, they said I needed another NEW CLUTCH, (and only 800 or so this time) I was so disgusted, I told em to put it back together, because I thought/think its a slave/master leak, not the clutch.  they told me "no, bad clutch" so I just took it home.   Well, after reading everything on every forum on this, I started from the front and slowly moving to the rear.  first, I took out the "master cyl" and discovered, they installed the banjo conector loop side down, not UP like everyone says it should be.<BR>who knows what else I will find as I move on back.||||reg||5
